<section class="container pagehead pagehead--narrow">
  <span class="kicker">Privacy &amp; cookies</span>
  <h1 class="pagehead__title">What we keep, and <em>what we don’t.</em></h1>
  <p class="pagehead__blurb">Written for readers, not lawyers. ME News Ireland is the data controller; the Data Protection Commission in Dublin is the supervisory authority.</p>
</section>
<div class="container prose">
  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p><b>Essential:</b> <code>me_session</code> keeps you signed in (30 days, HttpOnly). <b>Your choices:</b> <code>me_county</code> remembers the county you picked and <code>me_loc</code> a rounded position (about 100 m) if you shared your location; both live only in your browser and are never saved to an account. <b>Voting:</b> <code>me_voter</code> is a random id so you can change or withdraw a Signal or poll vote; it is not linked to you. Theme and text size are stored in your browser’s local storage. There are no third-party tracking cookies.</p>
  <h2>Location</h2>
  <p>Sharing your location is optional and can be forgotten from the county picker at any time. We use it once to find the nearest Irish town and county; we do not keep a history and we do not send it to anyone else.</p>
  <h2>Accounts and reports</h2>
  <p>An account stores your name, email, home town and county, and what you follow. Community reports store what you submit, an optional photo or video, an optional GPS position and, for guest reports, the contact you gave us so we can confirm it. Uploads stay private until an editor publishes them. Photo metadata (EXIF) is read to help editors verify a report and is stripped from published images.</p>
  <h2>Email alerts</h2>
  <p>Alert sign-ups store your email, county, optional town and which alerts you asked for, plus the time of the last morning email. Every email carries a one-tap unsubscribe. Sign-ups are confirmed by email before anything is sent.</p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>Adverts are served by us from our own database. We count impressions and clicks per advert; we do not profile readers, and no advertising network sees your browsing.</p>
  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>Card and PayPal payments are handled by Stripe and PayPal. Card numbers never touch our servers; we store a customer reference and the subscription status.</p>
  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>Wire headlines are kept for a limited period and then pruned. Community reports and notices remain published until withdrawn or expired. Server logs are kept for 30 days for security.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for a copy of your data, correct it, or have it deleted by emailing <a href="mailto:<?= e($contact) ?>"><?= e($contact) ?></a>. Deleting an account removes your profile, follows and sessions; published reports are withdrawn unless there is a public-interest reason to keep them, which we will explain. You can complain to the <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Data Protection Commission</a>.</p>
</div>
